{
  "id": "grammar.a1.123.a",
  "title": "Size and colour",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Which size, which colour?",
      "content": "*Méret* is size and *szín* is colour. To ask about size, use *milyen*: *Milyen méret kell?* (What size is needed?) You know *kell* with a noun: the answer names the size, with no *-t*: *Nagy kell.* (A large one is needed.) To ask which colour, use *melyik*: *Melyik szín kell?* Too big or too small? Say *túl*: *Az ing túl nagy.*"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Size and colour",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Milyen méret kell?",
          "What size is needed?"
        ],
        [
          "Nagy kell.",
          "A large one is needed."
        ],
        [
          "Kicsi kell.",
          "A small one is needed."
        ],
        [
          "Melyik szín kell?",
          "Which colour is needed?"
        ],
        [
          "Az ing túl kicsi.",
          "The shirt is too small."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "Examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Milyen méret kell?",
          "english": "What size is needed?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Milyen színt kér?",
          "english": "What colour would you like?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Nagy kell.",
          "english": "A large one is needed."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "A kabát túl nagy.",
          "english": "The coat is too big."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "A cipő túl kicsi.",
          "english": "The shoe is too small."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "*Kell* with a size has no *-t*: *Nagy kell*. Only the colour you ask for or buy takes *-t* in a full sentence: *Milyen színt kér?*"
    }
  ]
}
